idated Democratic-independent challenge could narrow the margin, though not plausibly the outcome.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Brad Little (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Idaho's governor race is one of the least competitive in the country. Republican incumbent Brad Little, renominated without difficulty, faces Democrat Terri Pickens, independent John Stegner, a Libertarian, and a Constitution Party candidate in a state that favored Republicans by about 18 points at the presidential level. Little has campaigned low-key while his opponents seek a breakthrough, including criticism of a nuclear innovation campus deal.\n\nEvery available signal points the same direction: all seven expert raters call the race Solid or Safe Republican, prediction markets give Little roughly a 97 to 98 percent chance, and the two polls of the race show him ahead by 10 and 21 points. Republicans also hold the fundraising lead in every statewide race. The main uncertainty is the size of the margin, not the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0111, "margin": -14.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0115, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0087, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0158, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0168, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0122, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.015, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0193, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0165, "margin": -14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0058, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0101, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0244, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.014, "margin": -14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0158, "margin": -14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0196, "margin": -14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.006